<misterromdescription>
    <name>Battle Tryst (ver JAC)</name>
    <setname>btltryst</setname>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <year>1998</year>
    <manufacturer>Konami</manufacturer>
    <rbf>KonamiM2Tryst</rbf>
    <buttons names="Button 1,Button 2,Button 3,Start,Coin" default="A,B,X,Start,Select" />

    <!--
      Battle Tryst's own build (KonamiM2.qsf's Battle Tryst lines), as KonamiM2Tryst_<date>.rbf in _Arcade/cores: the Z buffer in the SDRAM board's memory, compressed texture loads, the
      MPEG unit's control, and the CD's data sectors streamed from the mounted image. As Heat of Eleven's MRA, with RAM 2 x 8 MB and an
      M48T58: index 3 is its 8 KB, then a byte for the board: bit 0 the larger RAM, bit 1 the CD's data sectors streamed from the mounted
      image (the data track is 367 MB). Index 1 is only the drive's answers that aren't sectors (2048 bytes). The MPEG intro's pictures
      aren't decoded: it shows black.

      btltryst_cd.zip and btltryst_full.bin aren't in a MAME set; from the set's 636jac02.chd:
        chdman extractcd -i btltryst/636jac02.chd -o x.cue -ob x.bin
        python3 tools/fullimage.py x.cue btltryst_full.bin            (422,546,208 bytes, with btltryst_full.cue: in games/btltryst)
        python3 tools/cdimage.py chdman btltryst/636jac02.chd btltryst_cd.bin, with its header option (2048 bytes)
        zip btltryst_cd.zip btltryst_cd.bin                            (beside btltryst.zip)
      Main releases up to 20261010 don't mount btltryst_full.bin from here: choose it once under "CD audio image" in the OSD.
    -->

    <file delay="1" type="s" index="0" path="btltryst_full.bin"/>

    <rom index="0" zip="btltryst.zip" md5="none" address="0x30000000">
        <part name="636a01.8q" crc="7b1dc738"/>
    </rom>
    <rom index="1" zip="btltryst_cd.zip" md5="none" address="0x32000000">
        <part name="btltryst_cd.bin"/>
    </rom>
    <rom index="2" zip="btltryst.zip" md5="none">
        <part name="93c46.7k"/>
    </rom>
    <!-- the EEPROM, the service menu's settings: Main saves it (nvram/) and loads it in place of the set's 93c46.7k -->
    <nvram index="2" size="128"/>

    <rom index="3" zip="btltryst.zip" md5="none">
        <part name="m48t58"/>
        <part>03</part>
    </rom>
</misterromdescription>
